# Commit Message Format

All commits in this repo follow this strict format:

```
<JIRA> <type><scope>: <title>

<body>
```

## Required parts

- **JIRA** — `[NVMESH-NNNN]` (or concatenated brackets for multiple tickets, e.g. `[NVMESH-1][NVMESH-2]`), or `[NO-REF]` when there is no ticket. The bracketed form is always used so the no-ticket case has the same shape as a normal Jira reference.
- **type** — one of: `feat`, `fix`, `chore`, `style`, `docs`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `back/port`.
- **scope** — `(component)` for normal commits (e.g. `(BL)`, `(GUI)`, `(vpg)`, `(sanity)`, `(META)`), or `[ORIG-JIRA]` for `back/port` commits (the original ticket being ported).
- **title** — one-line summary, imperative mood, ≤ 72 chars. Required for every non-ported commit. Concretely names the behavior changed; avoid generic wording like "fix bug" or "address JIRA".
- **body** — extended description on a separate paragraph. **Mandatory for every commit.** Bullet the observable effects of the diff (conditions it applies to, what it preserves, what it intentionally skips). **Every paragraph in the body must start with `* `** (asterisk + space); paragraphs are separated by a blank line. A single paragraph is acceptable for a truly trivial commit (typo, rename), but never commit title-only.

## Grammar rules

- **No space** between `<type>` and the scope: `fix(BL)`, not `fix (BL)`; `back/port[NVMESH-4000]`, not `back/port [NVMESH-4000]`.
- The colon between scope and title is always present when a title is included.
- Body is separated from the title by exactly **one blank line**.
- Every paragraph in the body starts with `* ` (asterisk + space). Wrapped continuation lines of the same paragraph are not re-prefixed; the `*` marks the start of a paragraph, not each line.

## Type inference from JIRA

When the commit references a JIRA ticket, the commit type is inferred from the JIRA issue type:

| JIRA Issue Type                       | Commit type |
|---------------------------------------|-------------|
| Bug / Defect                          | `fix`       |
| Story / New Feature / Improvement     | `feat`      |
| Task / Sub-task                       | `feat`      |
| Epic                                  | `feat`      |
| Chore                                 | `chore`     |
| Tech Debt / Refactor                  | `refactor`  |
| Documentation                         | `docs`      |
| Test                                  | `test`      |
| Performance                           | `perf`      |
| Back-port / Backport                  | `back/port` |

If the issue type is unknown or ambiguous, ask the user to choose. For multi-ticket commits, the first JIRA's type drives the choice.

## Trailers

- `Change-Id:` and `Signed-off-by:` are kept when present.
- `Made-with:` (e.g. `Made-with: Cursor`) must **not** appear in committed messages. If it has been injected, strip it before the commit lands on a remote.

## Examples

**Standard (feature, BL component, with body):**

```
[NVMESH-1234] feat(BL): add stripe alignment for striped EC

* Round stripeSize up to the nearest block set so per-chunk allocations
  land on whole stripe boundaries.
```

**Bug fix, GUI:**

```
[NVMESH-9999] fix(GUI): disable submit button while form is validating

* Prevent duplicate submits when the user double-clicks during async
  validation.

* Re-enable the button on validation completion or error.
```

**Multiple JIRAs:**

```
[NVMESH-1][NVMESH-2] fix(GUI): align modal close button with form layout

* Wrap the close button in the form footer so it stays aligned when the
  modal grows.
```

**No JIRA reference:**

```
[NO-REF] chore(BL): bump eslint to 8.57

* Pick up new default rules; no code changes required after the bump.
```

**Back-port (original JIRA replaces the component):**

```
[NVMESH-4250] back/port[NVMESH-4000]: restore compatibility for pre-2.1 clients

* Cherry-pick of NVMESH-4000 onto release/3.4. No behavioral changes beyond
  the original fix.
```
